.TH SM-LLM-PROXY 1 2026-11-16 "sm-llm-proxy 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sm-llm-proxy \- logging OpenAI-compatible proxy that pins reasoning effort
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sm-llm-proxy
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR addr ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-upstream
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-\-log
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-reasoning-effort
.IR level ]
.RB [ \-\-reasoning-effort-none ]
.RB [ \-\-max-tokens
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sm-llm-proxy
is a small local reverse proxy for OpenAI-compatible chat APIs, written for the
self-hosted supermemory server.  It forwards every request to
.I upstream
verbatim, with three exceptions:
.IP \(bu 2
For
.B /chat/completions
requests it injects
.B reasoning_effort
unless the caller already set one.  DeepSeek models default to high effort,
which makes tool-looping agents expensive; supermemory never sets the field, so
this pins it.
.IP \(bu 2
It adds
.B stream_options.include_usage
to streaming requests so the final SSE frame carries token counts.
.IP \(bu 2
It can optionally cap
.B max_tokens
to a maximum value.
.P
Every response
.B usage
block is appended as one JSON object per line to
.I log
(JSONL), including prompt, completion, reasoning and cached token counts, the
model, message count, tool count and request duration.  The log is the cost
ledger for anything sitting behind the proxy.
.P
The request body is otherwise forwarded byte-for-byte, including the
.B Authorization
header.  Streaming responses are relayed as they arrive.
.P
A
.B GET /healthz
on the proxy answers locally with
.BR {"status":"ok"} .
.P
Defaults: host
.BR 127.0.0.1 ,
port
.BR 8787 ,
upstream
.BR https://api.deepseek.com ,
log
.BR ~/.local/share/sm-llm-proxy/requests.jsonl ,
reasoning effort
.BR low .
Environment variables
.BR SM_PROXY_UPSTREAM ,
.BR SM_PROXY_LOG ,
.BR SM_PROXY_REASONING_EFFORT ,
.B SM_PROXY_MAX_TOKENS
and
.B SM_PROXY_TIMEOUT
provide the same defaults.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " addr"
Address to bind (default
.BR 127.0.0.1 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
Port to bind (default
.BR 8787 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-upstream " url"
Base URL of the real API, for example
.BR https://api.deepseek.com .
A path component is preserved and prefixed to incoming paths.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " file"
JSONL file receiving one record per completion (default
.BR ~/.local/share/sm-llm-proxy/requests.jsonl ).
Parent directories are created on demand.
.TP
.BI \-\-reasoning-effort " level"
Value injected as
.B reasoning_effort
(default
.BR low ).
Use an empty string to disable injection.  DeepSeek accepts
.BR low ,
.B high
and
.BR max .
.TP
.B \-\-reasoning-effort-none
Shortcut for sending
.B reasoning_effort=none
to turn thinking off entirely.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-tokens " n"
If a request has no
.B max_tokens
or asks for more than
.IR n ,
rewrite it to
.IR n .
Default is no cap.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Upstream socket timeout (default
.BR 900 ).
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Log each proxied request to stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
Point the supermemory unit at the proxy:
.EX
Environment=OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1

systemctl --user restart sm-llm-proxy supermemory
.EE
.P
Watch token spend per agent step:
.EX
tail -f ~/.local/share/sm-llm-proxy/requests.jsonl |
  jq -c '{ts,model,prompt_tokens,completion_tokens,reasoning_tokens}'

jq -s 'map(.completion_tokens // 0) | add' \\
  ~/.local/share/sm-llm-proxy/requests.jsonl
.EE
.P
Temporarily disable thinking for a test run:
.EX
sm-llm-proxy --reasoning-effort-none --port 8788
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/sm-llm-proxy/requests.jsonl
Default usage ledger (one JSON object per request).
.SH NOTES
The proxy does not terminate TLS and binds to loopback by default; expose it
only on a trusted interface.  Responses are relayed with
.BR "Connection: close"
framing, so keep-alive is not reused.  Upstream failures return HTTP 502 with a
JSON error body.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR jq (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
